# __PROJECT_NAME__

A [brust](https://github.com/AssetsArt/brust) app: React components compiled ahead of time, served by Rust.

## Run

```bash
bun install
bun run dev        # brust dev routes.tsx (hot reload)  ->  http://127.0.0.1:1337
```

Scripts: `dev` (`brust dev`, with hot reload), `build`, `start`, `typecheck`, `dev:cf` (build for Cloudflare Workers and run `wrangler dev`), `deploy:cf` (build and `wrangler deploy`).

## Layout

- `routes.tsx` — `defineRoutes`: one layout, one page.
- `components/Layout.tsx` — the document root (`<html>` + `<Outlet/>`).
- `components/Counter.tsx` — a `useState` counter; the compiler makes it a native component (no React in the browser).
- `actions.ts` — an Elysia 2 app on `brust()`, served by Rust under `/_brust/action` (enabled by `[actions]` in `brust.toml`).
- `public/` — static files, served at `/public/...`.
- `wrangler.jsonc` — your Cloudflare bindings (D1, KV, vars); brust owns `main`, `assets` and `compatibility_date`.

## The hello action

```bash
curl 'http://127.0.0.1:1337/_brust/action/hello?name=ash'
# {"message":"Hello, ash!"}
```

From the browser, use the typed client:

```ts
import { client } from '@brust/core/client'
import type { App } from './actions'

const api = client<App>()
const { data } = await api.hello.get({ query: { name: 'ash' } })
```

